Normalize targets before training (per-label z-score), train on normalized y, then de-normalize predictions at inference; this alone often stabilizes multitask regression.

Normalize prosody features using train-set stats only (mean/std over all train segments), then apply same stats to val/inference.

Switch MSELoss to SmoothL1Loss (Huber) to reduce sensitivity to noisy labels/outliers.

Use a smaller model if data is limited: try d_model=64, num_layers=1, dropout=0.1, weight_decay=1e-4 (current setup may be over-regularized/underfitting).

Add an LR schedule (OneCycleLR or cosine decay with warmup) instead of fixed LR.

